Subject: [PATCH] tb710fu: persist COM5 CDC across all kernel panics and halts

Remove the nested assert(panic_info) in PE_update_panicheader_nested() when
gPanicBase == 0 (which previously hit nested panic limit 5 and bypassed
halt_all_cpus()), and enter tb710fu_cdc_panic_loop() before kPEPanicRestartCPU
so COM5 stays live for log drain and hands-free edl/reboot on every panic.

diff --git a/pexpert/arm/pe_init.c b/pexpert/arm/pe_init.c
index fd449f7..20377d9 100644
--- a/pexpert/arm/pe_init.c
+++ b/pexpert/arm/pe_init.c
@@ -737,8 +737,7 @@ PE_update_panicheader_nestedpanic()
 	 * if the panic header pointer is bogus (e.g. someone stomped on it) then bail.
 	 */
 	if (!panic_info) {
-		/* if this happens in development then blow up bigly */
-		assert(panic_info);
+		/* No iBoot panic VRAM region on TB710FU; avoid nested panic so CDC panic loop stays reachable. */
 		return;
 	}
 
